>> title: Singapore Mei Fun
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: noodles, curry, shrimp, pork, chinese, wok
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: singapore mei fun, singapore mai fun, singapore noodles, rice vermicelli, xing zhou chao mi, 星洲炒米
>> pairs-with: madras-curry-powder, char-siu
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min

>> step: soak 10 min, drain, loosen with your hands
Soak @rice vermicelli{8%oz}(225 g; thin) in hot water for ~soak{10%min}, until bendy but not soft, then drain them and pull the nest apart with your hands.

>> step: stir the curry sauce smooth
Stir @Madras curry powder{1%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{2%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, @sugar{1%tsp}, @chicken stock{1/4%cup}(60 mL), and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} together in a bowl.

>> step: scramble 1 min, into coarse curds
Scramble @eggs{2%large}(beaten) in @peanut oil{3%Tbs} in a hot #wok{} for ~fry{1%min}, breaking them into coarse curds.

>> step: stir-fry 3 min, shrimp just opaque
Stir-fry @shrimp{8%oz}(225 g; peeled), @char siu{4%oz}(115 g; julienned), @onion{1/2%medium}(sliced), @red bell pepper{1%medium}(sliced thin), and @bean sprouts{1%cup}(90 g) with @&(~1)egg{} for ~stirfry{3%min}, until the shrimp are just opaque.

>> step: toss over high heat 2 min
Toss @&(~4)noodles{} and @&(~3)curry sauce{} into @&(~1)wok{} over the highest heat the hob gives, lifting and folding with tongs for ~stirfry{2%min} until the strands are evenly yellow, then scatter @scallions{3}(cut in 2-in lengths) over.
